Z||000004||BAM-BAM||06-09-2000||11:32 PM||||   Batboy, I prefer the AIM-7 or AIM-9 Ground Platform Mounted Guided Nuclear Missle Battery (GPMGNMB) as opposedd to the 50 Cal Gattling Gun. For one, when incorporated with the Heads Up Display (HUD) system out of the 95+ Grand Prix, tracking and aquisition are a snap! Also, if you integrate an arming ON/OFF and trigger assembly to the shift handle (either auto or stick) you enjoy the freedom of OMNIPOSITIONAL SURVALENCE (OPS) while remaining in complete control of the Battery Platform (BP) at all times. This will ensure an unparralled Kill to Incodent Ratio(KIR) while allowing necessary Terminal Mental Agression Discharge (TMAD). Once the opposition is concious of Your GPMGNMB you will notice an incresed Respect To Presence (RTP) ratio. This is merely my suggestion on the use of a prooven deterent to Inatentive Behavioral Disorder (IBD). Good luck..... This message will self destruct in 5 seconds...<P><BR> Later, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000005||Shiner||06-10-2000||01:13 AM||||This is my golden driving rule, and it has gotten me past the "I'm 16-18 and I wrecked a car!" thing which everyone seems to do.  The rule?  Assume that other drivers will do the worst possible thing at the worst possible time.  I am usually not disapointed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierospeeder||12-31-1995||09:19 PM||||You should have made another post,<BR>Idiot drivers part IV<BR>i think that was the last one we left of on.<P>I almost got side swipped by a van that wanted to switch lanes, while i was in that lane.  This was three blocks away from my house, i was in the right lane, and i guess the driver realized theres a fiero driving on gravel and he went back into his own lane.  SUV drivers are the worst, they love tailgating my fiero.  I get more respect driving my tbird, but i still get morons that think they own the road, or want to take chances.  Chicago is planning on banning cellular phone use on the roads, its still being debated, some of the police superintendents were saying that it would be to much work for them, in pulling over everyone.  Some people were saying why dont we pull over people, reading,eating etc.. <P>I was riding my motorcycle, and had one guy on a phone, driving in the middle of the white line, while his left turn signal was on, eventhough he turned right. I guess its like a blonde who cant walk because shes chewing gum at the same time!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||06-10-2000||10:10 AM||||Using those blasted cell phones when you're driving is a big pet peeve of mine too. If their window is down I usually yell at them to "JUST HANG UP AND DRIVE!" I get lots of dirty looks and flipped off too. Kansas City is the worst around here. They go screaming by you at 20 MPH over the speed limit in their BMW's, switching lanes in and out of traffic, with that STUPID phone glued to their ear. Talk about an accident waiting to happen.||||reg||1
Z||000008||deceler8||06-10-2000||11:44 AM||||Your post makes me wonder why no one has ever tried to install some defensive measures in the pop up headlights. Imagine...someone pisses you off, you hit the headlight switch, the lights pop up, and you hit the "fire" button on the gearshift handle, and a la Mad Max, your adversary is a smoking tangle of twisted metal and plastic.<P>Man, I gotta start drinking decaf...||||reg||1
Z||000009||Uaana||06-10-2000||12:48 PM||||Ditto what everyone else said.<BR>My GF thinks that it's just my driving and that she never has probs with suv's and the like. <BR>On thursday I had yet another run in with an Expidition, (btw you should need at least a class B lisc to drive something that big) I'm trapped in a middle lane but going slightly above the speed limit and for 3mi i get tail gated by the damn thing. well I give him a salute out the sun roof and start to do the sports car shuffle and this idiot actually tries to keep up. Well I left him pinned in the slow lane with a semi on his ass.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>As for payback devices..<BR>Someone mentioned zipstrip in the windshield washer tank with outlets on the rear of the car.<BR>High intensity (read 300w) backup lights mounted under the B pillar overhang. that you could toggle at will.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||tgowens||06-10-2000||01:16 PM||||what I want to do is turn my wing (on my '87GT) into a mirror that I can pivot up when those bozos with the tall trucks get behind me with their brights on -- not only would it block the light out of my car but it would reflect their lights back in <I>their</I> face!!! I could then drive away from the stoplight and leave them sitting there!!||||reg||1
