Z||000012||Shadow Wolf||06-11-2000||02:58 AM||||I find the GT wing does a good job blocking the headlights at night actually.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I've had minivans ride my backend in snow..  A couple years back I was driving a sprint and was actually ploughing in front of the car, and this damn 4x4 PASSES me on a country backroad... ... about 6 inches from the driver side mirror.||||reg||1
Z||000013||RFMike||06-11-2000||11:20 AM||||KC can't be any worse than Minneapolis/ St. Paul in rush hour.  Last week, I'm doing my commute thru downtown St. Paul, in the left lane.  Solid traffic across 4 lanes, six feet of shoulder on my left, and concrete wall at the edge of the shoulder.  The guy in the Lexus to my right is yakking on a cell phone, and I'm in his blind spot.  Nothing I can do about it, I'm locked in.  Next thing I know, he starts into my lane, no turn signal, no look, just go.  I slow down, but the guy behind me was tailgating, and he's gonna hit me, so I ease over onto the shoulder.  I'm blowing the horn the whole time.  The Lexus finally hears me, and stays halfway in my lane.  He eventually gets enough room between myself and the car in front of him to force his way in.  This all happens very quickly.  <BR>When I pull alongside the Lexus, he flips me off!  I have been relatively calm until this point, because I have mostly gotten used to idiot exposure.  This one really bugs me.  I'm wishing I had my old 3/4 ton diesel pickup, with the rusty body.  NOBODY messed with me when I drove that.  Big, loud, and ugly.  I could have had a sign that said, "Hit me, I want a new truck.  Just be ready when I bash you back."<BR>Unfortunately, I'm not, and I like my GT, so I shake my head and let him go.<BR>I have concluded that there is no hope for the terminally stupid, and they are able to obtain a driver's license.||||reg||1
Z||000014||batboy||06-11-2000||11:40 AM||||All this talk just gave me a great stupid idea. My 86 Suburban has 270k miles, rusted out, been basically totaled from hail damage, and now the tranny is failing again. Estimates to rebuild the 4X4 700R4 tranny range from $950 to $1200, which is probably more than the ol' gal is worth. It's been a great truck, but I'm afraid it's on it's last legs. Lots of things going wrong with it. Next person that pulls out in front of it or cuts me off, I'm afraid I might not be able to hit the brakes fast enough. Let their insurance pay for it and teach 'em a lesson both at the same time...hmmmm...I like it!<P>Better yet, next tailgater with a fancy expensive car (with airbags) that rides my rear bumper...well, a "dog" might run right out in front of me causing me to slam on my brakes... sorry dude, but you ran into the back of ME! Hope you have good insurance!<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 06-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Raydar||06-11-2000||10:00 PM||||Does anybody know if automatic trans fluid will kill a catalytic or an O2 sensor?<BR>Thinking about plumbing a supply of the stuff into my intake system, controlled by a switch. <BR>Ever been behind a car with a bad modulator valve on the auto trans? <BR>Smokes like a house on fire. <BR>Guaranteed to discourage tailgaters.  ||||reg||1
Z||000016||batboy||06-11-2000||10:29 PM||||It'd be a good guess that the cat won't like tranny fluid. You need to inject it past the cat. BTW, I was joking about my last post, just in case anyone was wondering. I'd never risk injurying even an idiot driver and I sure would NOT mention it on a public forum even if I did intend on doing it. I ain't stupid.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Patrick's Dad||06-11-2000||11:02 PM||||Actually, I used to have a single use weapon for tailgaters in winter. With fresh snow on the Fiero, I could drive along the highway, get some jerk in the rearview, and just smile. At the right time, I'd poke the headlamps on. The air would carry the snow now raised into the airstream, and into the jerk's windshield. They usually back off after that....||||reg||12
Z||000018||fierospeeder||06-12-2000||02:21 AM||||I hate SUVs, <BR>but i always loved trucks.<P>I was going to buy a S-10 or a truck instead of my tbird.  <P>But i really wanted was a 1980 Chevy silverado.  6inch suspension lift, 3 inch body lift, Very high resistant tires, 30 inches tall?  winch in the front with a very large steel bumper.  I decided for the car, because the mods to do this are expensive.  I think i probably would have finished it already with the money i put in cars.  <BR>My headlights would going into some Yuppy's SUV rearview mirror.<P>JC whitney sells amplified microphones, and truck i mean semi truck horns, i planned on getting a horn and putting it in my car.  The microphone is good for saying something to some idiot.<P>I purchased a motorcycle recently.  83 nighthawk, i forgot the actual numbers but its about 12 seconds 120mph in a 1/4 mile.<BR>but i can get off the line at any light very quickly and i will be going 10 over the speed limit.  I will get the usual idiots that think they are quicker because they are driving 20 over the speed limit and pass me.  The other idiots, you pass them going 10 mph over the limit but not exceeding and later you notice they pull up to you drive next to you for a while, after a few seconds they pass you going faster then you.<P>Caniball run had james bond releasing oil into other cars, the car with pac man in it had smoke, it was a total ricer car for the 80s.||||reg||1
Z||000019||dodger||06-12-2000||02:51 AM||||I'm with you guys on this subject. It didn't occur to me it's because I'm in a small car.(maybe I'm a little dense)<BR>But when I'm doing 5mph over the limit and there's a good chance of cops around, and a suv or truck runs up on me when there's no traffic around, he (or she!) can take a flying **** before I'll move over... ||||reg||1
Z||000020||BN Boomer||06-12-2000||04:05 AM||||I hate little sports cars. Everybody who owns one either believes themselves to be Mario Andretti weaving in and out of heavy rush hour traffic just to get an extra car length ahead or they hog the left lane, drive 5mph over the speed limit, and are too much of a rude a$$hole or just plain ignorant to display even the slightest amount of common courtesy and move to the right when being overtaken by another vehicle.<P>Hopefully this sounded about as intelligent as the previous 2 responses above.<P>Get over it people, it not what is being driven, it's who's doing the driving. In one of my past incidents on the road, I once almost mashed a nice Mercedes into the guardrail because the guy was driving like an idiot while trying to merge onto the freeway. He finally backed off. Guess I should blame it on his car, right?||||reg||8
Z||000021||DaRkLoRD||06-12-2000||04:16 AM||||what I REALLY HATE is people who go slow.. move over and motion for you to pass.. and when you do, then they speed up, and don't let you pass, but if you try to get back in behind them.... then they slam on the brakes and don't let you back in behind them.<P>I was heading out to a friends house in another friend's van, and these 2 old idiots in a green pickup truck did that to us.. we were almost killed cause the oncoming traffic didn't slow down either.. we had maybe 1-2 seconds to spare when we finally got back into the correct lane.... if they were other teenagers, that'd be different.. but these were literally old people.... almost killed a minivan full of teenagers... WTF are people like that doing with licenses?????||||reg||1
Z||000022||ThatRickGuy||06-12-2000||11:29 AM||||Ahh the Joys of driving a '76 Lemans, 2.3 US Tons of rolling vengence. I find that a 7 ft wide front bumper and high beams do a pretty good job of getting people out of the fast lane. But all in all, I avoid doing stupid stuff. In Japan, there are people know as drifters, they have nice, hoped up ricers, and they tilt their licence plates at 45 degrees (so the bottom sticks out) They would weave threw traffic, doubling the speed limit, driving scary as he&#0124; &#0124;. But at least they were good at it, never saw one of them even get in a fender bender. Out here on the east coast, just south of DC, we have I-95, and people are just crazy out here. I had a buddy get hit by someone trying to "drift" at over 85 miles an hour (in a 55!) And I know I've almost been hit numerous times. Something I'd like to see is the US switching to a driving system more like Germany. it cost about $2-3,000 to get a licence, you have to be 18, pass numerous test, extencive training time. But you look at thing like the autobon. The rummors of "no speed limit" isn't exactly true. Only the left lane is no speed limit, and it is ONLY used for passing. just driving in the fast lane w/o anyone in the next lane is a massive offence, passing on the right is also a big no no, drifting, or reckless driving is also harshly punished. And if someone is in front of you, and you want to get in front of them, you turn on your left turn signal. No honking, screaming, brights, or tailgating, and let me tell ya, they are smooth out there! Very few accidents as compaired to the US, and if you paid 3 grand for your license would you risk it???||||reg||1
Z||000023||BN Boomer||06-12-2000||12:28 PM||||In a country that is considerably more vast with less public transportation available and therefore far more dependant on personal automobiles than typical European countries, I think such an exorbitant amount just to get a license is way too burdensome. It would also serve to further stratisfy us economically, which I do not believe is a good thing. Given the Europerans propensity to tax everything into oblivian, I'm not so sure I want to emulate them too closely. $5 for a gallon of gas, anyone? <P>I think more driver training and experience are the biggest keys to improving driving skills. The current trend towards a system of graduated licenses as young people gain experience will help in creating better drivers. More stringent test requirements would be a step in the right direction as well.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Raydar||06-12-2000||01:03 PM||||I think it's really sad that the only requirements for getting a license in the US (depending upon local laws), are to:<BR> <BR>(1)Be at least 16. <BR>(2)Pass a written test. <BR>(3)Be able to parallel park. Once.<BR>(4)Be able to drive around a parking lot without killing any cones. Once.<P>*Having a pulse is recommended, but not mandatory.||||reg||1
Z||000025||bHooper||06-12-2000||02:38 PM||||Uaana, what a great idea, about useing lights.  A person could rig up light's to a photovoltaic switch, so that when it was hit with enough light... pow, on comes your "anti-light" light!<P>As for drivers and particular vehicles... I drive a Jeep Cherokee (which is a SUV).  I think most people, today, just don't know how to drive... with the exception of minivan drivers... they are <B>ALL</B> idiots!||||reg||1
Z||000026||Gold-86SE||06-12-2000||04:37 PM||||<BR>Throwing in my 2 cents.<P>I believe that the biggest problem that we face is, yes, uneducated drivers.  However, on top of that you add to the problem when (generally speaking here, with a broad brush) many police departments only cite drivers for speeding.  Give me a break. Speeders are not the only traffic offenders.<P>A few years back I was permitted to driver 70 mph in a 55 zone, if I paid the ghastly tax on speeders.  I had the pleasure of wasting my time and everyone elses in the local courtroom.  While there, I spoke with the DA regarding speeders paying the highest percentage of tickets and not really being the biggest problem on the road.  His response was very enlightening. He stated plainly and unapologetically(sp) that speeders are pulled over simply because of ease of prosecution, because speeders stand out in the crowd. The black sheep is easy to spot amongst the non black sheep, so to speak.<P>There are those that recklessly speed down the interstate and yes they give the high speed drivers a bad name.  But speeding is not the cause of problems on the nation's highways.<P>The number one accident cause on the roadways is speed.  Hello. Anybody home? Anytime you are driving a vehicle you speed, because with out speed the auto would not move.  This is stupid category, and should be eliminated. The other main causes of accidents are following too closely and driving under the influence.<P>Eliminate these and the culprits are those who a) don't have the talent or mental ability to properly drive, and b) those who want to play traffic cop.<P>Culprit "a" is fairly easy to spot because they contribute to most of the offensive problems on the highway, which the defensive driver will avoid.<P>Culprit "b" on the other hand, thinks that no one, repeat NO ONE, has the right or priviledge to drive in any manner but the manner culprit "b" deems fit.  This is complete barbara strisand.  Take for example "road rage."<P>What exactly is road rage? Simply put it is one driver who aggrivates another, and both get in a shoving match.  Reporters, Judges, and the rest of the "system" want to target high speed drivers and the cause of road rage, when this is a false pretense.<P>How many times have you been driving down the road, minding your own business, paying attention to the traffic speed, the posted speed and everything else, but you get some wacko head case that believes that they should prevent you from getting to your destination, for whatever reason?  You did not instigate this road rage by your speeding, yet some dip stick thought he would get his jollies by harrassing you.<P>This part of road rage is never given any air time in reports, printed page space, or controlled by the local police.  I have witnessed many more road rage instances caused by this, than speeding. Yet speeders are blamed for all road problems, just like guns are blamed for all gun related deaths.<P>Someone stated earlier that it is not the vehicle that causes the problem, but the driver, which very true.  But the real problem we have, as drivers who like to performance drive, is that officials will not take to task the responsibility to make the roads safe to all drivers.<P>It is more important to the system to have as many cars on the road as possible because of the taxes that are collected on the autos.  Solving road problems is not a concern of officials and as long as we preformance driver we will pay the additional tax, regardless.<P>I would propose my solution to this mess, but that would double the space I stole, but thanks for letting me rant, and vent.<P>Gold-86SE has stepped down from the soapbox, mimicing "Elvis has left the building."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000027||DJRice||06-12-2000||04:43 PM||||Caniball Run???<BR>James Bond???<P>I dont remember the movie quite like that...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000028||DJRice||06-12-2000||04:45 PM||||Batboy, <P>If you get a chance, wander on to ebay and do a search for "Hot Wheels Sting Rod."<P>Based on your comments in the first post of this thread, you will get a kick out of what you see!||||reg||1
Z||000029||BlackGT||06-14-2000||03:42 PM||||Hey Batboy,<BR>I feel you`re pain! I deal with those situations on Atlanta`s roads every day<BR>while going to and from work so I know how<BR>you feel. I grew up in New York City and <BR>used to think those drivers were crazy but<BR>since moving to Atlanta I realize that most<BR>operators suffer from "head in the a$$ syndrome". There is no road test here to get a license and most of these morons are clueless and brain dead idiots with cell phones. Rules of the road and common sense<BR>go out the window here. My girl asks why I never do the speed limit...I demostrated why,<BR>I got into the middle lane kept the speed at <BR>60 told her to watch what happens......every<BR>a##hole and their mama tried to drive over me or thru me. I really love the (I don`t mean to offend anyone with a pickup) rednecks<BR>in pickups and mommies in explorers who insist on driving so close I can count the number of teeth they`re missing! What I used<BR>to do when I rode my motorcycle was carry marbles in my pocket just for them and when<BR>they did something real stupid or just tried<BR>to piss me off I would toss a handfull over my shoulder. It would get their attention real fast when they hear crack crack crack<BR>on their front end or windshield and just about<BR>all of them would back the hell off me. <BR>It`s dangerous, cheap but a very effective<BR>deterent to stupid drivers!!||||reg||1
Z||000030||fierospeeder||06-14-2000||08:10 PM||||just got a motorcycle, i should go buy some marbles.  <P>In illinois, there is a written test, piece of cake for me, and a driving test, which involves going onto the street, turning a few times and going in reverse.  No parallel parking.   <P>I must have been pulled over 6 times for speeding in two years, only three tickets, 2 warnings, and one let go, cause it was raining.  I mostly drive only 10mph over the speedlimit, to avoid being pulled over.  What i hate seeing is when im going 50 in a 40mph limit, i see people going a lot faster then me and not getting a speeding ticket.  Speeding tickets are expensive, and i do agree that, why dont bad drivers get tickets for no turn signals, tailgating, aggressive driving??  <P>There should be an advance driving school, like there is with motorcycles.  Those who graduate get a E on their license ,expert, and a sticker on their front and rear bumper or window to identify to the police that we are capable in handling a vehicle such as a professional driver would.||||reg||1
Z||000031||87GTBro||06-14-2000||11:12 PM||||On a lighter note:<P>I think Fiero's are invisible when they are on the road.  People always pull out in front of me, but it is no problem because I just go around them and honk the horn as I do.  Usually I am traveling so fast that my GT is just a little red blurr to people and they are afraid to pull in front of me.<P>But my big problem is not other cars.  I find that birds like to swoop down in front of my car as I am driving down the road.  There can be absolutely no birds on the road in front of me and then all of a sudden I am looking at the rear end of a bird fighting to get out of the way before it splatters on the windshield.<P>But WHY IS IT that when the car is parked out in the open, the birds always seem to find it when they have to relieve  themselves.  I don't understand it.||||reg||1
Z||000032||wkayl||06-15-2000||12:13 AM||||I used to have an 83 Monte Carlo Diesel.  When anyone tailgated me I would just floor it.  It wouldn't go any faster, but boy would it pump out the black smoke.  I made an old dodge van back off more than a 1/4 mile in rush hour traffic one time.  No one else wanted to pull in behind me.||||reg||1
Z||000033||Deer_Slayer||06-15-2000||12:53 PM||||Charleston WV is as bad as the towns mentioned above.  The thing I would like to see is these people (yuppy women especially) try to retake their driver's tests in their SUV's.  I gurantee a lot of them would fail.  ||||reg||1
Z||000034||Raydar||06-15-2000||06:59 PM||||I think it would be interesting, in the case of an especially large SUV rear-ending an especially small car , due to tailgating, if some enterprising D.A. would decide to charge the SUV driver with Assault With a Motor Vehicle. It may not "stick" every time, but if the word got out, it would sure give folks something to think about.  ||||reg||1
Z||000035||007DOUG||06-15-2000||10:39 PM||||batboy.<P>Watch those metros, they pack a punch. I have to drive the company 2000 metro everyday. It will do 100 mph. Takes three days to do it, and has to be on level ground. <P>Mine will do 100 only because it the base model. NO Air, No Radio. That saves weight. <P>There is one race metros will beat us at.........mileage. I totally thrash mine, and it still gets 40 mpg. And with gas at $1.75.....||||reg||1
